---

<Doc
  title="Accessibility"
  kicker="Accessibility"
  updated="October 12, 2026"
  description="FutureClarity Technologies wants everyone to be able to use its website. The standard we aim for, how we test, and how to reach a person if something gets in your way."
>
  <p>
    We want everyone to be able to use futureclaritytechnologies.com and book a free audit, including
    people who use a screen reader, a keyboard, voice control, magnification or captions.
  </p>

  <div class="summary">
    <h2>Need help right now?</h2>
    <p>
      Call or text <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      We'll book your audit, answer questions, or send anything on this site in another format.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What we aim for</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA. In practice, that
    means:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A clear page structure with headings, landmarks and a "Skip to content" link.</li>
    <li>Every form field has a visible label, and errors say what to fix.</li>
    <li>Text contrasts with its background, and links aren't marked by color alone.</li>
    <li>Everything works with a keyboard, with a visible focus outline, including the cookie choices.</li>
    <li>Pages reflow on small screens and when text is enlarged, without sideways scrolling.</li>
    <li>Photos have text descriptions, and decorative images are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li>No flashing content, and the site respects your device's "reduce motion" setting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we test</h2>
  <p>
    We check pages with automated accessibility testing (axe) and by using them with only a keyboard, on
    desktop and phone screen sizes, and we re-check when we make changes. Automated tools can't catch
    everything, so we also welcome reports from the people who use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Known limits</h2>
  <p>
    Google's cookie and analytics tools, which load only if you allow them, and the websites we link to
    are run by other companies, so we can't promise how accessible they are.
  </p>

  <h2>If something doesn't work for you</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us what page you were on and what went wrong, and we'll fix it or get you what you need another
    way. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or call or text
    <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>. We aim to reply within two business days.
  </p>

  <h2>The sites we build</h2>
  <p>
    The websites and dashboards we build for clients are held to the same standard, and we're happy to
    talk through accessibility for yours.
  </p>
</Doc>
